    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The hamlet’s railroad station is one of the easternmost major stops on the LIRR Montauk Branch, linking New York City to the East End.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.longislandguide.com/visit/speonk/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1897 the LIRR catalog noted that “Speonk” sounds like a frog’s call, a quirk conductors loved to repeat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speonk%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area once hosted thriving duck farms in the 1880s, though most disappeared by the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speonk%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Speonk sits beside Moriches Bay, giving residents easy access to boating and fishing on the South Shore.",
